W</given-names></name><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Rowland</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Worrall</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>MacDonald</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kilian</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Scaling-up and sustaining insecticide-treated net coverage</article-title><source>Lancet Infect Dis</source><year>2003</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>465</fpage><lpage>466</lpage><comment>discussion 467&#x02013;468.</comment><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12901886</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1473-3099(03)00717-5</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>WHO</collab></person-group><article-title>Scaling up insecticide treated netting programmes in Africa</article-title><source>WHO/CDS/RBM/200243</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>World Health Organization</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>NETMARK</collab></person-group><article-title>Public-private partnership for sustainable malaria prevention</article-title><year>2004</year><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.netmarkafrica.org/ITNs/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schellenberg</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Abdulla</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Minja</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Nathan</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Mukasa</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Marchant</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Mponda</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Kikumbih</surname><given